      {
        "narration": "Eight people sealed themselves in and started suffocating slowly. Nobody could work out where the oxygen was going.",
        "visual_query": "large glass greenhouse arizona desert",
        "visual_fallback": "glass greenhouse"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Biosphere 2 is three acres of sealed glass in Oracle, Arizona. The crew went in on the twenty-sixth of September, 1991.",
        "visual_query": "sonoran desert mountains arizona morning",
        "visual_fallback": "desert mountains"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Sixteen months in, oxygen had slid from 20.9 percent to 14.5. That is the air on a four-thousand-metre mountain, indoors.",
        "visual_query": "indoor rainforest biome glass roof",
        "visual_fallback": "indoor rainforest"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The answer was the building. Carbon dioxide was reacting with bare concrete, turning into calcium carbonate and locking the oxygen into the walls.",
        "visual_query": "bare concrete wall structure interior",
        "visual_fallback": "concrete wall"
      },
      {
        "narration": "They grew 83 percent of their food and still lost a sixth of their body weight. Meanwhile the cockroaches and ants did fine.",
